<title>POLAND: NBP drains PLN 1.8 bln from Polish money market.</title>
<headline>NBP drains PLN 1.8 bln from Polish money market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 1.8 billion zlotys from the market through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction after banks bid to place the same amount with the central bank, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained the market for 14 days at an unchanged maximum rate of 22.15 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
